    "Colin's searches, replayed every night after build_web and against the live API by search_regressions.py.",
    "Part C, 16 Sep 2026: Colin searched 'QLD under $750k' and was shown a Victorian lot filed as Queensland and a lot a later read said was On Hold, while three real Shape Homes lots in Walloon sat hidden. Each brief below is one of his searches or one of the form slips that turned a search into 0 results; 'expect' is what must hold for it.",
    "Plan section 5 numbers the briefs (#1-#14); critique #20(d) adds QLD <= $800k. Critique #12 replaces #13's brief. No links, no client details: hashes are content_hash prefixes, the Dawn lots are named by estate, lot and price (critique #3: either twin may survive).",
    "7 Oct 2026: vic_any, nsw_any, qld_any and sa_any are the state-wide, no-budget searches Coleen compares with E-Agent, each with the obvious-rows check; hook_shaped_vic_any is the widest brief Clare's hook sends. On the 6 Oct database the 600-row candidate cap showed 322 of VIC's 2,837 obvious lots; search_regressions now fails any search the cap cut, any obvious row past the needs-confirming pages, and any response over 4 MB.",
    "8 Oct 2026: act_any, tas_any and nt_any are the same state-wide search for the states the form offers since that night, and wa_any for the one state it offered that the replay never searched. The first live parity counted 207 obvious ACT lots (Proxima: The Grande, Ahlei, Cento) that no state search could reach by name.",
    "28 Sep 2026: v2:43802e2d (18491, Howard lot 21, 'Available') is no longer in never_in_a_qld_search. It was listed because on 16/09 a LATER read of the same line (v2:d9553ad6, 15953) said On Hold -- a fact about the order of two reads, which the replay's sibling invariant checks from the data every night. G Developments' own list then read the lot 'Available' on 27/09 and 28/09, and the On Hold line was last seen 24/09, so the fixed entry failed 30 checks a night on a lot that is for sale again. 15953 stays listed: that capture is On Hold."
